<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n326" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγᾰνακτ-έω</span></b> , properly in physical sense,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>feel a violent
			irritation,</i> of the effects of cold on the body, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Liqu.</u>
				2
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Heliod.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				46.7.8
			</span></i>; of wine, <i>ferment,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.734e
			</span></i>; so metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεῖ τε καὶ
			ἀ.,</span> of the soul, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				251c
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>to be displeased, vexed,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδ᾽ ἀγανάκτει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					287
				</span></i>
			; esp. <i>show outward signs of grief,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κλάων καὶ ἀ.</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phd.</u>
				117d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ σπλάγχν᾽ ἀγανακτεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					1006
				</span></i>
			, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐνθυμούμενος</span> . .
				<i><span class="en">
				And.
				4.18
			</span></i>:—foll. by a relat., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ.
				ὅτι</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				4.2.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				3.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. εἰ . . , ἐάν</span> . .
				<i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.139
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>La.</u>
				194a
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c. dat. rei,
				<i>to be vexed at</i> a thing, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θανάτῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					63b
				</span></i>
			, etc.; c. acc. neut., ib.<i><span class="en">
				64a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ταῦτα, ὅτι</span> . . <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Euthphr.</u>
				4d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐπί τινι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					1.1
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				16.49
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρ τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Euthd.</u>
					283e
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					349d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διά τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					63c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Epict.
					<u>Ench.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				M.Ant.
				7.66
			</span></i>; and sts. c. gen. rei, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				334
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>to be vexed at</i> or <i>with</i> a person, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					5.3.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρός τινα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cam.</u>
					28
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Diog.Oen.
				68
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατά τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Tim.</u>
					18
				</span></i>
			:—c. part., <i>to be angry at,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀποθνῄσκοντας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					62e
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				67d
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Med.
			 in act. sense, aor.
			part.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ησάμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Somn.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Palaeph.
				40
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠγανάκτηνται τῷ πράγματι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					70
				</span></i>
			.</div>
